    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d720">

                <pb facs="0687" n="589" xml:id="pg589"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Choate.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-02-19"><hi rendition="#italic">February 19,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 308.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence
                    relative to the seizure of American flour and other merchandise off the east
                    coast of Africa by British men-of-war, and with reference particularly to the
                    Department’s No. 286, of the 26th ultimo, specially relating to the claim of the
                    Pennsylvania Milling and Export Company, I inclose, for your further
                    information, copy of a letter from the president of that company commenting upon
                    their shipments and stating that they sent nothing directly or indirectly to the
                    Transvaal.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d720-a1.xml" xpointer="d720-a1"/>
